# Copy to infra/backup.env on the server (gitignored, like server/.env) after
# running `rclone config` as the deploy user to set up a remote — see the
# manual steps printed by infra/server-setup.sh.
#
# Format: "<remote-name>:<bucket-or-path>". E.g. a Backblaze B2 remote named
# "b2" with a bucket "englisher-backups" is RCLONE_REMOTE=b2:englisher-backups.
# Works the same way for AWS S3, DigitalOcean Spaces, Cloudflare R2, or any
# other rclone-supported backend — only this line changes.
#
# Leave unset (or don't copy this file) to keep backups local-only.
RCLONE_REMOTE=
